# Accepted findings for the container image scan (.github/workflows/docker.yml,
# Trivy: HIGH/CRITICAL with a fix available fail the build).
#
# Every entry needs a reason, written on the line(s) above it:
#   - why the finding does not apply to this image (the vulnerable code path is
#     unreachable, the package is present but never executed, …) or why it is
#     accepted for now;
#   - who accepted it and when, plus the issue tracking its removal;
#   - an expiry where Trivy supports one (`exp:YYYY-MM-DD` after the ID), so an
#     acceptance is re-reviewed rather than becoming permanent.
#
# Example:
#   # libfoo in the Debian base; the image never invokes it (no shell
#   # pipeline reaches it). Accepted 2026-11-17, tracked in #NNN.
#   CVE-2026-00000 exp:2027-02-17
#
# An entry with no reason is a finding hidden, not accepted — reviewers should
# refuse it. Prefer fixing (rebuild on a patched base) over listing here.
